(7223115, 1113256, 45524, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m kind of at the point where if I see one more guy, naked in the corner to express "emotion" or "vulnerability" I think I''m going to scream. Also, it''s hard to see this as an avatar. Also, I''m pretty sure I can see part of your junk. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I literally LOL''d at this loud enough I scared the dog.</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: I''m kind of at the point where if I see one more guy, naked in the corner to express "emotion" or "vulnerability" I think I''m going to scream. Also, it''s hard to see this as an avatar. Also, I''m pretty sure I can see part of your junk.   I literally LOL''d at this loud enough I scared the dog.', '2014-06-01 01:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7224114, 1113121, 58634, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by charlene9797:</b></div><hr/><i> Ugh I wish I knew how to focus the eyes! I guess using my remote would have helped </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If you use a tripod or a set place for the camera to be when taking the picture, you can put an item where your eyes (or other desired focused object) would be and manually focus it and leave the lens focused. Afterwards, place the intended item in front of the camera and voila!<br/> <br/>It might take some trial and error but with practice you''ll get the gist of it. <br/> <br/>Aside from the out of focus aspect, this is a lovely image with great composition :)</td>', 'Originally posted by charlene9797: Ugh I wish I knew how to focus the eyes! I guess using my remote would have helped   If you use a tripod or a set place for the camera to be when taking the picture, you can put an item where your eyes (or other desired focused object) would be and manually focus it and leave the lens focused. Afterwards, place the intended item in front of the camera and voila! It might take some trial and error but with practice you''ll get the gist of it.  Aside from the out of focus aspect, this is a lovely image with great composition :)', '2014-06-03 16:52:00.000000', NULL, 0),
